			<div class="content" id="post-content-4850398">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> vehicle / extradimensional / ad-astra</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A dead space ship from the future, which has an invisible entity on board that can kill in atmospheric environment and is sentient.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The SCP is divided into 2 parts, the ship (SCP-XXXX) and the entity (SCP-XXXX-1). The ship is an advanced human design (not Foundation) that at the current time should not exist. The crew has been killed either by the entity or during venting atmosphere (attempt to kill the entity by the captain). One of the Foundation researchers notes a couple of things about the ship including a device that appears to allow travelling through spacetime using another dimension. Also there is one body missing.</p>
<p>The entity was not on the ship when it engaged its device. It either came from the travel-dimension or said dimension altered a crew member (or both). It can be heard walking around the ship and is pretty harmless in void. It can jump between ships and when in any atmosphere, arms may come from the walls, pulling people &quot;inside&quot; the walls and killing them in the process (they are basically split into their atoms). This is an attempt to pull people into its &quot;dimension&quot;, hinted to be an communication attempt.</p>
<p>The Foundation team sent to explore the ship finds the original crew dead, some melted to the ships structure. After a while a team member is killed by the entity (accident with suit leads to air escaping) and more die during the escape due to friendly fire and a hull breach. 2 survive and try to communicate with the entity (that can understand visual things like guestures but not writing) while they slowly run out of oxygen and there is no help coming soon.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The entity on board the ship is only dangerous under atmospheric pressure but humans need that to survive. It might not be hostile on purpose.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Hopefully this hasn't been done before.</p>

