<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi Galcedion. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>So I like the fact you’re attempting to write a sci-fi scip, doubly so that it involves horror. My main problem with the concept is that it’s the basic plot of almost <em>every</em> Hollywood alien movie out there, mainly: crew goes on a mission, encounters alien they don’t understand, get murdered one-by-one etc. At this point, the genre is tried, tested, and cliqued, to be honest.</p>
<p>I know you’ve tried to give the alien more distinguishing characteristics, but still, the other dimension aspect is from <em>Event Horizon</em>, the melting of the crew into the walls is a page lifted from <em>Aliens</em>. What I’m saying is that the best way to distinguish a sci-fi scip from others is know what’s already out there and have a different origin story of your entity, if you’re sticking with the horror. Right now, you’ve said it’s “unknown”, and that just won’t cut it either. Encourage you to expand on this a little more.</p>
<p>If you decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll take another look. For now, all the best!</p>

							</div>

								
					
