<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I&#8230;really don't know about this? There's hints of intriguing elements: like the entity being invisible and harmless unless it's in atmosphere, and that the entity was one of the former crew, but the actual core of the narrative here just feels like an exceedingly generic murder monster story; and I feel like it could be fixed if this was just&#8230;shifted a little to be less horror orientated.</p>
<p>Like, consider if this was the story about someone being alone in space for so long that it changed them, and the focus was a lot more in how they react once they're no longer alone but they don't really know how to interact with the world any more; where perhaps you still keep the horror elements present but the motivation is this eldritch thing trying to interact with a world it's no longer part of and doing harm accidentally and that like, causing it to hate what it's become and stuff; and then you have this ending moment where like, everyone realises what has happened and it's like&#8230;bittersweet because they understand but they don't know what they can do to stop it?</p>
<p>Also&#8230;have you considered whether a SCP is the best format for this? It feels to me that a lot of the trappings of a SCP article (e.g., the ConProcs, leading with the Description) would make this story a lot more awkward to tell; whereas something like a tale from the perspective of one of the crew members might work a lot better. You wouldn't necessarily have to change a lot of the plot beats for this; including the presence of the Foundation, but it'd allow you to really focus on the important stuff and also to not worry about how to answer the question of 'how does anyone know what happened here'.</p>
</div>
